# Copy to `.env` in this directory and fill in what you need.
#   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored. A real exported environment variable always wins over this
# file, so a release script can set POPPY_ADULT without a stale .env fighting it.

# ── Sign in with Google ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An OAuth *client id*, not a secret: it is public and appears in the page. There is
# no client secret in this flow.
#
# Create one: console.cloud.google.com
#   1. Pick or create a project.
#   2. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen → External → fill in app name, support
#      email, developer email. Add yourself under Test users while it is unpublished.
#   3. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID
#      → Application type: **Web application**
#   4. Authorised JavaScript origins — add every origin the app is served from:
#        http://localhost:8000     (./run.sh)
#        https://your-domain       (once deployed)
#      No redirect URI is needed: this flow returns the token to the page.
#   5. Copy the "Client ID" (ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com) below.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Content switches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Three separate decisions. See backend/config.py for what each one actually does.
POPPY_ADULT=1          # 1 = adult content, no platonic steer, no brevity cap
POPPY_GUARDRAILS=0     # 1 = "I'm an AI" honesty line + supportive/no-advice steer
POPPY_CRISIS_LAYER=1   # 1 = self-harm detection and the helpline card. Leave it on.

# ── Model ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ollama tag for the desktop/web build. The abliterated 3B is what makes adult mode
# work; a stock model will refuse whatever the prompt says.
# OLLAMA_MODEL=huihui_ai/llama3.2-abliterate:3b-instruct

# ── Data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WITHOUT this, ./run.sh writes your real companion data into the repo root.
# Set it for anything that is not your own everyday use.
# POPPY_DATA_DIR=/tmp/poppy-qa
